From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 01:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: restore the UFS Apps SMMU stream

The temporary UFS SMMU bypass was sufficient to reach the root filesystem
after constraining DMA to 32 bits, but buffered OSTree imports still make the
device enter Qualcomm crashdump without a preceding Linux panic or UFS error.
The same class of abrupt failure on DWC3 was resolved by restoring its Apps
SMMU attachment and selecting a translated domain.

Restore the upstream SM8150 UFS stream ID while leaving the currently failing
ICE dependency disabled. The conditional no-iommus DMA workaround remains in
the source but no longer applies to this node.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -239,7 +239,7 @@ &spss_mem {
 };
 
 &ufs_mem_hc {
-	/delete-property/ iommus;
+	iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x300 0>;
 	/delete-property/ qcom,ice;
 };
 
-- 
2.50.1
